// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6111 Add rule: potential NTLM authentication coercion tool execution
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6111
// Pull request author: ashish-cybersec
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential NTLM Authentication Coercion Tool Execution
// Sigma ID: bfda903c-f36f-432b-ae0f-fba97afc34a8
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Ashish Pulivarthy (ashish-cybersec)
// Date: 2026-07-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1187
// Description: Detects execution of tools that coerce NTLM authentication by abusing Windows RPC interfaces.
//   These tools force a target machine, typically a Domain Controller, to authenticate to an
//   attacker-controlled listener with its machine account. The captured authentication can then be
//   relayed, which may lead to full domain compromise. Covered tools are DFSCoerce (MS-DFSNM),
//   ShadowCoerce (MS-FSRVP), WSPCoerce (MS-WSP) and Coercer, which automates coercion over multiple
//   RPC interfaces.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/Wh04m1001/DFSCoerce
//   - https://github.com/ShutdownRepo/ShadowCoerce
//   - https://github.com/RedTeamPentesting/wspcoerce
//   - https://github.com/p0dalirius/Coercer
//   - https://blog.redteam-pentesting.de/2025/windows-coercion/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/d1ca98b84f59e42b7749477ea0cb2ffa791d26f2/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_ntlm_coercion_tools.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "DFSCoerce" or FolderPath contains "ShadowCoerce" or FolderPath contains "WSPCoerce") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "dfscoerce.py" or ProcessCommandLine contains "shadowcoerce.py") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "coercer coerce " or ProcessCommandLine contains "coercer fuzz " or ProcessCommandLine contains "coercer scan " or ProcessCommandLine contains "coercer.py coerce " or ProcessCommandLine contains "coercer.py fuzz " or ProcessCommandLine contains "coercer.py scan ")
